    {
      "id": "PB08",
      "finding": "Reorder itself does not cancel the active job. The inspected ordinary work/finish toils do not recheck ShouldDoNow each work tick or trim the produced batch to the target. Thus target count is a scheduling threshold, not a hard output cap, and an in-flight batch can overshoot. Long UFT work explicitly checks job override after3000ticks on1000tick hash intervals, so absolute never-preempted semantics are not established.",
      "xml": [
        "PBX03"
      ],
